# Flash and NVS dumps from this unit are NEVER committed.
#
# They contain the operator's Wi-Fi PSK and pool credentials in cleartext —
# `DcentAxeConfig` documents that the default NVS partition is unencrypted, and
# the AxeOS "main" namespace stores `wifipass` the same way. This mirrors the
# standing rule for held vendor factory dumps: reference them by SHA-256, never
# commit their contents.
#
# The stock backup is also 16 MB, which does not belong in git regardless.
# Its SHA-256 is committed (`stock-full-16mb.bin.sha256`) so the restore
# artifact stays verifiable, and `extract_nvs.py` + `make_nvs.py` reproduce
# every derived file from it.
stock-full-16mb.bin
stock-nvs.bin
stock-nvs-dump.txt
stock-nvs-extracted.json
live-nvs.bin
live-nvs-extracted.json
live-nvs.json
stock-nvs.json
new-nvs.bin
new-nvs.csv
nvsval_*.txt
themecolors.txt
